     "result_text_tail": "2023 increase caused.\n\n**Things to know before you use it:**\n- **No slide preview:** no slide-to-image tool was available and the sandbox blocked Keynote, so I haven't seen the slides. The renderer reports no layout problems, but please flip through the deck before presenting.\n- **Assumptions:**\n  - The 60% enterprise cap applies equally to contracts renewing in 2027.\n  - Trailing retention holds through 2027.\n  - Customer churn rates are applied to ARR.\n  - The pack gives no cost for the onboarding programme.\n\n  Each assumption is listed on its slide and in the workbook.\n- **QA:** all checks pass with one warning: the pack says \"about three times\" in words, so the script can't match the figure 3.\n- **Data:** every number traces to the briefing pack: 52 taken from it directly, 56 calculated from those, and 14 marked as estimates with their basis shown. No placeholders remain.\n\n**Choices I made where I'd have asked you:** audience is the CEO and leadership team approving the plan in December; theme is navy; I approved the storyline myself. The 10% and 8% steps match the tested and precedent levels. I set enterprise at 7% for all renewals for simplicity; the higher-ARR alternative is 10% on uncapped contracts.\n\nI can switch the theme, or rework the growth-target slide once new-customer bookings data is available.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- palisade-pricing-2027.pptx\n- palisade-pricing-2027-sources.xlsx\n\nThe spec and its build script are in `work/` if you want to re-render."
